<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.3.4: Finding the Solutions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02119</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.3.4: Finding the Solutions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>71265944-c197-4d67-86dc-69295f89335c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Student Activity</title>
<para>Use what you have learned in the lesson to solve the following quadratic equations.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(5m^2= 80\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(m=4\) and \(m=-4\)</para>
<para>\(5m^2=80\)</para>
<para> \(\frac{5m^2}{5}=\frac{80}{5}\)</para>
<para> \(m^2=16\)</para>
<para> \(m=\pm \sqrt{16}\)</para>
<para> \(m=4\) and \(m=-4\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((m−6)^2=100\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(m=16\) and \(m=-4\)</para>
<para>\((m−6)^2=100\)</para>
<para>\((m−6)=\pm \sqrt{100}\)</para>
<para>\(m−6=10\;\;\;\;m−6=-10\)</para>
<para>\(m =16\) and \(m =-4\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(\frac{2}{3}y^2−8=−2\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y=3\) and \(y=-3\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}\frac23y^2-8&amp;=&amp;-2\\\frac23y^2&amp;=&amp;6\\\frac32\left(\frac23y^2\right)&amp;=&amp;\frac32\left(6\right)\\y^2&amp;=&amp;9\\y&amp;=&amp;\pm\sqrt9\end{array}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(\frac{1}{6}(x+3)^2−8=16\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=9\) and \(x=-15\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}\frac16\left(x+3\right)^2-8&amp;=&amp;16\\\frac16\left(x+3\right)^2&amp;=&amp;24\\\left(x+3\right)^2&amp;=&amp;144\\\left(x+3\right)&amp;=&amp;\pm\sqrt{144}\end{array}\)</para></section>
</content>
